Saccade tail and lost-gaze ease for the eye-tracked focus (native/quadviews/dcsvr_gaze.h, which explains them; tested by
tests/quadviews-gaze; ported from GitHub PR #26). New keys, all off when absent (the filter as before):
dcsvr_saccade_tail=1 (the lead's saccade ends below dcsvr_saccade_end_speed instead of dcsvr_saccade_speed, its leading
edge never retreats during one saccade, repeated tracker samples are not speed samples; the plain saccade other code
reads stays on dcsvr_saccade_speed) and dcsvr_lost_ease_ms (without a gaze past Quad Views' cache the focus slides to
the fixed one over this time instead of jumping; 0 off). Each located focus box is recorded for the landing check, and
the 30 s gaze line adds landings, landings outside the sharp area, repeated samples and eases.
